# JavaScript Standards

## Function Declarations

Use arrow function syntax for all functions instead of the `function` keyword.

```javascript
// ❌ BAD
function calculateTotal(items) {
  return items.reduce((sum, item) => sum + item.price, 0);
}

// ✅ GOOD
const calculateTotal = (items) => {
  return items.reduce((sum, item) => sum + item.price, 0);
};
```

This applies to standalone utility functions, React components, event handlers, and callbacks alike.

```javascript
// ❌ BAD
function ThoughtsTest() {
  return <div>...</div>;
}

// ✅ GOOD
const ThoughtsTest = () => {
  return <div>...</div>;
};
```

